/-!
# A spanning tree adapted to the three-cycles in the Fi23 action

Every nontrivial cycle of the second generator contributes two consecutive
edges. Breadth-first search using the first generator connects these cycles.
The packed records contain a parent letter, an edge label, and a depth.
Local descent and action equations, checked below, prove that the tree covers
all letters; no external orbit or stabilizer assertion is trusted.

Source: retained ATLAS F23G1-p31671B0 tables, in the inverse-cycle convention.
Application: the first prefix bound for GLS3 Table 5.3u. Reproduce with
`First/source/generate.py`.
-/

set_option Elab.async false

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Fischer.Fi23.CentralizerSection.FirstTree
